WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.069
We just got the first teaser trailer for Wreck-It
Ralph 2 and hidden in there are some sneaky

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:09.890
Disney easter eggs including Aladdin's lamp,
Star Wars favourites Yoda and Chewbacca, plus

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.390
our first look at Ralph breaking the internet.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.530
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and this is my Wreck-It Ralph 2 trailer breakdown

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:20.320
for all the Disney and movie references you
might have missed.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.550
Don't forget to let me know about any other
cool details you spotted in the comments below.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.189
Thanks to footage shown at D23 last year,
we already know that the Wreck-It Ralph sequel

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:34.640
is going to feature loads of characters from
other big Disney properties, one of which

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.680
is Lucasfilm's Star Wars.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:42.440
In fact, the D23 clip showed C-3PO and a bunch
of Stormtroopers, along with X-wings and TIE

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.340
fighters, all appearing in a sequence that
also included Disney's princesses, Dumbo,

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.370
and Iron Man!

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:52.590
Now, while we don't get to see those particular
Star Wars figures in the new trailer for Ralph

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.800
Breaks the Internet, there is a hidden hat-tip
to the galaxy far, far away in Mr Litwak's

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.739
office where, if you look closely at his shelves,
you'll see a couple of decorative plates featuring

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:08.680
none other than the little green Jedi Master
Yoda and Wookie co-pilot Chewbacca!

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:12.730
If you want to catch some other nice nods
to Disney movies, then check out the items

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:16.830
on sale in the background while Ralph and
Vanellope are staring at that cat painting

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:17.830
on eBay.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:23.320
There's a Magic Lamp like the one that appears
in Disney's 1992 animated musical Aladdin,

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.640
which is getting a live-action remake next
year with Will Smith starring as Genie.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:32.170
And there's also a Cast-Iron Frying Pan like
the one featured in Disney's animated movie

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.170
Tangled.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:36.830
Although its eBay listing only says that the
pan is 'great for everything from frying chicken

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:42.130
to grilling a tortilla', it can also make
a very effective weapon, as Rapunzel, Flynn,

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.340
and the Royal Guard all show very well during
the course of Tangled.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:53.560
"Oh, mama, I have got to get me one of these!"

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:59.350
When the arcade owner Mr Litwak uses his computer,
you can spot a reference back to the first

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.980
Wreck-It Ralph movie.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.500
Take a look at the bottom right side of the
screen and you'll find a document called "Letter

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.500
to Nana".

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.990
In the first film, Litwak mentions his senile
nana several times:

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.080
"Mr. Litwak!"

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.270
"What's the trouble, sweetheart?"

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:14.360
"Oh, boy!"

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.740
"Look's like the game's gone cuckoo, like
my nana!"

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.640
"I'll have someone look at it in the morning,
but if he can't fix it, it may be time to

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.800
put old Ralph and Felix out to pasture.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:21.800
Like my nana!"

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.800
"Sorry, sweetie.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:23.800
Here's your quarter back."

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.800
"But what about the game?"

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.800
"I'll have someone look at it tomorrow..."

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.840
"But if he can't fix it, it might be time
to put old Ralph and Felix out to pasture."

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.410
"Like my nana."

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:35.730
The final pancake scene of Ralph feeding a
poor bunny so much it explodes seems like

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.280
a tease of Ralph doing what the movie's title
says: breaking the internet.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.990
The little girl who was playing the pancake-milkshake
game until Ralph took over was certainly horrified

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:45.990
when she saw the bunny explode!

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:46.990
"Eat, eat!"

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:51.890
"Er, Ralph, you might wanna try feeding the
kitty for a little while."

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:52.890
"No!

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:53.890
The kitty gets the milkshake."

00:02:53.890 --> 00:03:00.940
"The bunny gets the pancake."

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:08.530
"Eeehhhh"
This scene also reminded me of similar moments

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:11.280
in the Willy Wonka and Monty Python movies.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.810
In Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory,
Violet Beauregarde blows up like a giant blueberry

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:20.050
after she takes Willy Wonka's experimental
3-course dinner gum.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:24.430
And the Wreck-It Ralph scene is also a call-back
to Mr Creosote, the glutton from Monty Python's

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.880
The Meaning of Life, who explodes after he
finishes an enormous meal with an after-dinner

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:29.880
mint.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:35.160
By the way, the little girl who Ralph traumatises
reminds me of Baby Moana from Disney's last

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.160
animated movie.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.900
And it might be a way of including a Moana
easter egg to repay the Wreck-It Ralph easter

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.870
egg that appeared in Moana.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.990
The older Moana will also be appearing in
a separate scene in Wreck-It Ralph 2 together

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.810
with a group of other Disney princesses.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:51.870
Although we didn't get to see them in this
teaser, hopefully they'll be in the next full

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:52.870
trailer.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:56.500
There's obviously going to be a ton of pop
culture references and online jokes in Wreck-It

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.500
Ralph 2.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.500
A couple that pop up in this trailer are fake
prize scams and clickbait articles.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.850
"Congratulations, you're a winner!"

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:03.850
"Really?"

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.930
"These 10 child stars went to prison!"

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:06.930
"Ooh."

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:07.930
"Number six will amaze you!"

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.930
"That sounds interesting."

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.630
Now, there's a good number of actors who've
ended up in jail, but I wonder if this could

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:16.370
be a jab at former Disney child star Lindsay
Lohan who's well-known for getting into trouble

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:18.229
with the law and has served time.

00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:22.499
As a child, Lohan starred in Disney films
such as The Parent Trap and some of the studio's

00:04:22.499 --> 00:04:27.770
TV movies, and, just last year, she suggested
on Instagram that she should play Ariel in

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:30.759
a live-action version of Disney's The Little
Mermaid.

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:34.689
Of course, given that Ralph and Vanellope
are exploring the internet, there's also bound

00:04:34.689 --> 00:04:37.069
to be some more adult-themed jokes in the
movie.

00:04:37.069 --> 00:04:41.580
I did notice that in the internet reception
hall, there's an IP Address Lookup area with

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:47.610
signs pointing to, among other things, "Unzip
Services" and browser "History Clearance".

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.210
And you can make what you want of that!

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.690
Just before I finish, I want to note that
we don't know a lot from this teaser about

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.699
what's going on back at the video arcade.

00:04:54.699 --> 00:04:58.900
From the brief shots of a very empty parking
lot, and the way things are lit inside the

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.689
arcade, plus the fact that Game Central Station
doesn't look very busy, there's a sense that

00:05:03.689 --> 00:05:08.779
the amusement arcade might be losing business
perhaps due to online competition.

00:05:08.779 --> 00:05:12.860
And a brief synopsis of the movie indicates
that Ralph and Vanellope have ventured online

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:16.190
to look for a replacement part for her game
Sugar Rush.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:20.270
So, let me know if you've got any theories
about what else you think might be going on.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.259
So, what did you think of the teaser trailer
for Wreck-It Ralph 2?

00:05:24.259 --> 00:05:26.370
And do you feel it looks as good as the first
film?

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:30.339
Let me know your thoughts in the comments
below and if you love animation, check out

00:05:30.339 --> 00:05:35.210
my recent Pixar videos on Incredibles 2 and
Coco by tapping the screen right here.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.669
And if you enjoyed this, don't forget to like,
share and subscribe to get all my new videos!

00:05:39.669 --> 00:05:42.069
Thanks for watching and see ya next time!

00:05:42.069 --> 00:05:43.329
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

